{:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532974} {:answer/id #uuid "42b0ce1a-0757-53db-93de-7de1b53bce5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532983} {:answer/id #uuid "5e22d1ff-80c3-5392-a495-c399a03b3ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532988} {:answer/id #uuid "89981f02-ad8a-513e-828a-e400b88e66d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0137e495-9519-563c-a9ee-6f5584f3dcad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532968} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0a0640-dade-51e4-9d76-499e8b522693" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532971}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ab52b6-83e6-54a5-afb6-55184c5bbcb6" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+4y}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{4y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{e}^{4y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x},\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n{e}^{-4y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "707a9662-a514-5dc4-bc0a-687d138a9a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{4+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532989} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdac19f-bf7b-5a5c-9d62-d0171d74c4d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{4+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532990} {:answer/id #uuid "a486f8f5-5d40-591c-b231-a3bd909c081a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532997} {:answer/id #uuid "c247858e-5af0-5089-b95b-c8d1999ef52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533002} {:answer/id #uuid "d3623e5b-41cb-51d2-908e-c2825e724307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x+2}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a486f8f5-5d40-591c-b231-a3bd909c081a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532997} :answer-field/id #uuid "08436a20-ac16-5134-98bd-17ac2d5fefc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532970}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81f64b39-6f57-500d-a5c6-3fe05e3c018a" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{12x+3x{y}^{2}+8+2{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5x}{(3x+2)(4+{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{3x+2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n(4+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a42831a-fc6c-505f-91db-624efe60589b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3+{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532972} {:answer/id #uuid "0b865beb-828e-5981-a26d-0adafc67630e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3+{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532973} {:answer/id #uuid "2d681c76-75f8-5a31-94d4-5eb6019d8fb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x+2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532981} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6814b3-8f36-5644-b687-0444e7abfc14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3+{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{2x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532987} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b26db0-5685-5fb2-ae27-fec1821c4f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{2x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4b