ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x+2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532994} {:answer/id #uuid "d87ff72b-4395-583b-be61-bc1afd372800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533006} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ff3107-a7d2-59db-8b09-67444edeaf28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2346f555-930d-5070-98b7-5e1217159460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532980} :answer-field/id #uuid "11a3a2ee-3214-5652-a1e8-c95275af79fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532976}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa110f6f-e8a3-5f93-ae17-13ecc7c36e75" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{9x+3x{y}^{2}+6+2{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{(3x+2)(3+{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3x+2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n(3+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{3x+2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11adaa5b-badb-5193-b9a8-c971ca877a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x+4}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532977} {:answer/id #uuid "13e25510-f32e-5583-a11d-67f2557629f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532978} {:answer/id #uuid "32262977-c1c8-542a-b231-36f8b3b5fc4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x+4)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532982} {:answer/id #uuid "90518027-c2da-59c1-9c70-ef4bd227b41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x+4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532995} {:answer/id #uuid "ba119bc6-c3f3-53de-9d41-a1e681290b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba119bc6-c3f3-53de-9d41-a1e681290b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533001} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9778fd8-3195-5e5f-8896-1f489905a54b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd63e6d3-9aec-5442-bf20-03fb4398eaba" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{6x+3x{y}^{2}+8+4{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5x}{(3x+4)(2+{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{3x+4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n(2+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{3x+4}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1636c696-c883-5327-b1d1-95d5845e693a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2+{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532979} {:answer/id #uuid "4afec3df-d25f-5250-be9a-b8e235f33d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+4)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2+{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532984} {:answer/id #uuid "50fd0c44-809b-56e8-bffa-64daf91f5728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x+4}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532985} {:answer/id #uuid "a0365396-629f-5676-a2ff-5f577f030cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x+4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2+{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532996} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd8ba74-f3ec-5ca8-a446-60f1b1676907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccd8ba74-f3ec-5ca8-a446-60f1b1676907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533004} :answer-field/id #uuid "a98e2cd8-e387-5cb8-a456-9bec570be0f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f80f43dc-927c-5fe3-8a83-f47ed23baef3" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{4x+2x{y}^{4}+8+4{y}^{4}}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5x}{(2x+4)(2+{y}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{2x+4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n(2+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+4}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}]}
